@chapter Filtering

Basic filtering is done by access-list.

@example
ip access-list deny 10.0.0.0/9
ip access-list permit 10.0.0.0/8
@end example


@node Route map, IPv6 supports, Filtering, Top
@comment  node-name,  next,  previous,  up
@chapter Route map

Route map is very usefull functionality of zebra.  There is match and
set statement in route map.

@example
route-map test permit 10
 match ip address 10
 set local-preference 200
@end example

This means if a route match ip access-list number 10 then set it's
local-preference value to 200.

